statement:
Let P, d ∈ ℕ, U ⊆ ℝ^P open, N ⊆ ℝ^P an embedded C² d-dimensional submanifold (IsEmbeddedSubmanifold 2 d N) with (N̄ ∖ N) ∩ U = ∅, and y ∈ N ∩ U. Then there are r > 0, c ≥ 0 and a map π : ℝ^P → ℝ^P such that:
- B̄_r(y) ⊆ U;
- π is C¹ on B_r(y) and π(B_r(y)) ⊆ N;
- π(x) = x for x ∈ N ∩ B_r(y);
- Dπ(x)v = v for x ∈ N ∩ B_r(y) and v ∈ T_xN. Here Dπ(x) is the Fréchet derivative of π at x, and T_xN = tangentSpace N x is the set of velocities γ'(0) of C¹ curves γ : (−1, 1) → N with γ(0) = x;
- ‖Dπ(x)‖ ≤ 1 + c|x − y| (operator norm) for every x ∈ B_r(y).
